# Keep the build context small and keep local state out of the image.
#
# The transparency log database is the important entry. A committed or copied-in log would
# be a dead snapshot of somebody's laptop whose roots were signed by the published demo
# key, shipped into a deployment that is supposed to build its own history.

.git
.github
.gitignore

# Local state and caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.remember/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Transparency log databases -- never bake one into an image.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

# Secrets. Nothing here needs one, so anything matching is an accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
service-account*.json
secrets.json

# The console is deployed separately (Vercel), so it is not part of the API image.
web/

# Not needed at runtime: the demos and tests import from `aegis`, which is installed, and
# the image is a service rather than a development environment.
tests/
demo/
docs/

# `results/` used to be here, and the JSON is now needed at runtime: /v1/real-model serves
# the committed measurements so the site and the repository cannot disagree about what was
# measured. Adding `COPY results` to the Dockerfile without this change copied nothing at
# all -- the build succeeded, the endpoint deployed, and it reported `measured: false`
# forever. Two files that have to agree, and the one nobody edited wins silently.
#
# Only the JSON is re-included. Anything else that lands in results/ stays out, and the
# *.sqlite3 rules above still apply, so a log database can never ride in this way.
results/*
!results/*.json
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.md
!README.md
